# Chip, Badge & Button Styling

All chips, badges, pills, tag elements, and buttons must use **`rounded-[4px]`** for corner rounding. Never use `rounded-full`, `rounded-md`, `rounded-lg`, `rounded-[6px]`, or `rounded-[8px]` on buttons or chips.

## What uses `rounded-[4px]`
- All `<button>` elements (primary, secondary, icon buttons, toolbar buttons, submit buttons)
- Status badges (active, archived, invited, pending, deactivated)
- Role badges (Super Admin, Team Leader, Coordinator)
- Tag/label chips in tables (NDIS number, diagnosis, relationship, role, department)
- Count indicators (filter counts, selection counts, sidebar nav counts)
- Invoice status chips (sent, paid, overdue)
- View pills / tab pills
- Display toggle chips (column visibility toggles)
- Format toolbar buttons (text editor)

## What does NOT use `rounded-[4px]`
- Toggle switch tracks and knobs → keep `rounded-full`
- Circular avatars/initials → keep `rounded-full`
- Loading spinners → keep `rounded-full`
- Small dot indicators (6px or smaller) → keep `rounded-full`
- Modal/dialog containers → keep `rounded-lg`
- Dropdown menus/popover surfaces → keep `rounded-lg` or `rounded-[6px]`
- Input fields → keep their current rounding
- Card containers → keep `rounded-lg`

## Standard button classes
- Primary button: `rounded-[4px] bg-blue-500 px-[8px] py-[4px] text-[13px] font-medium text-white transition-colors hover:bg-blue-600`
- Secondary button: `rounded-[4px] border border-[#bababa] px-[8px] py-[4px] text-[13px] font-medium text-[#262626] transition-colors hover:bg-[#f5f5f5]`

## Standard chip classes
- Status chip: `rounded-[4px] px-[8px] py-[1px] text-[11px] font-medium`
- Table cell chip: `inline-flex h-[28px] items-center whitespace-nowrap rounded-[4px] border border-[#bababa] px-[8px] text-[12px] font-medium text-[#262626]`
- Count badge: `rounded-[4px] px-[4px] text-[10px] font-bold`
